1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,001
Not everyone who uses your site should be able to do everything.

2
00:00:05,001 --> 00:00:09,574
Roles and permissions decide who can view, edit, publish, and manage what.

3
00:00:09,574 --> 00:00:14,490
In this video, you create a role, choose its permissions, and give it to a user.

4
00:00:19,090 --> 00:00:23,137
A permission is one thing a person may do, such as editing content

5
00:00:23,137 --> 00:00:25,892
that other people wrote, or managing users.

6
00:00:25,892 --> 00:00:28,140
Modules add their own permissions.

7
00:00:28,890 --> 00:00:32,222
A role is a named set of permissions, such as Editor.

8
00:00:32,222 --> 00:00:36,006
You grant permissions to a role, and then give the role to as

9
00:00:36,006 --> 00:00:37,700
many people as you like.

10
00:00:38,450 --> 00:00:42,693
A user can have several roles, and receives the permissions of all of them.

11
00:00:42,693 --> 00:00:47,040
When you change a role, you change what everyone who has it is allowed to do.

12
00:00:47,790 --> 00:00:50,245
Three system roles are always there.

13
00:00:50,245 --> 00:00:55,330
Administrator is allowed to do everything, and its permissions cannot be changed.

14
00:00:56,080 --> 00:00:59,777
Anonymous stands for every visitor who is not signed in.

15
00:00:59,777 --> 00:01:05,084
Authenticated stands for everyone who is signed in, and signed-in users receive the

16
00:01:05,084 --> 00:01:07,410
permissions of Anonymous as well.

17
00:01:08,160 --> 00:01:10,614
Every other role is yours to create.

18
00:01:10,614 --> 00:01:15,173
A site set up with the Blog recipe also has Author, Contributor, Editor,

19
00:01:15,173 --> 00:01:20,140
and Moderator, and modules grant default permissions to roles with those names.

20
00:01:24,423 --> 00:01:28,017
Roles are under Access Control, Roles in the admin menu.

21
00:01:28,017 --> 00:01:31,843
The page lists every role of the site, with its description.

22
00:01:32,341 --> 00:01:34,879
The three system roles carry a System badge.

23
00:01:34,879 --> 00:01:38,330
Every role has an Edit button, and only the roles that are not

24
00:01:38,330 --> 00:01:40,361
system roles have a Delete button.

25
00:01:40,849 --> 00:01:46,338
Edit on Administrator opens a page with a notice instead of a list of permissions.

26
00:01:46,338 --> 00:01:50,329
This system role already grants all available permissions.

27
00:01:50,803 --> 00:01:54,773
Anonymous and Authenticated are edited like any other role.

28
00:01:54,773 --> 00:01:59,903
Whatever you allow there applies to every visitor, or to every signed-in user.

29
00:02:00,412 --> 00:02:03,712
Opening this page takes the View Roles permission.

30
00:02:03,712 --> 00:02:07,660
A user who has View Roles but not Manage Roles sees the list,

31
00:02:07,660 --> 00:02:10,782
without the Add Role, Edit, and Delete buttons.

32
00:02:11,242 --> 00:02:14,831
Adding, editing, and deleting roles takes Manage Roles.

33
00:02:14,831 --> 00:02:19,832
Both are permissions like any other, so you give them to roles in the same way.

34
00:02:24,132 --> 00:02:27,443
Let's create a role for someone who proofreads posts.

35
00:02:27,443 --> 00:02:32,102
Add Role opens the Create Role page, which asks for a Name and a Description.

36
00:02:32,636 --> 00:02:36,321
We name the role Proofreader, and describe what it is for.

37
00:02:36,321 --> 00:02:40,986
A role name must be unique, and it cannot be changed after the role exists.

38
00:02:41,441 --> 00:02:44,593
Create saves the role and returns to the list.

39
00:02:44,593 --> 00:02:49,501
Save & Configure saves it and opens its permissions, so let's use that one.

40
00:02:53,720 --> 00:02:58,329
Permissions are listed in groups, usually one for each feature that provides them.

41
00:02:58,329 --> 00:03:01,420
Each row has an Allow column and an Effective column.

42
00:03:01,877 --> 00:03:06,504
No permission is allowed for this role, but View all content is effective.

43
00:03:06,504 --> 00:03:09,684
Allow means the permission is granted explicitly.

44
00:03:09,684 --> 00:03:16,567
Effective also counts permissions implied by another one, and permissions granted by Anonymous and Authenticated.

45
00:03:17,024 --> 00:03:19,631
Search permissions narrows the list.

46
00:03:19,631 --> 00:03:23,727
Let's search for access admin, and allow Access admin panel.

47
00:03:23,727 --> 00:03:29,004
A user needs this permission, from any of their roles, to use the admin at all.

48
00:03:29,464 --> 00:03:33,617
Next, search for list content and allow List content items, so the role

49
00:03:33,617 --> 00:03:35,343
can open the content list.

50
00:03:35,343 --> 00:03:39,658
Then search for edit content for others and allow Edit content for others,

51
00:03:39,658 --> 00:03:43,164
which lets the role change content written by other people.

52
00:03:43,616 --> 00:03:47,310
Some rows carry a Security Critical badge, like Manage Roles.

53
00:03:47,310 --> 00:03:51,831
Such a permission could let a user elevate their other permissions, so grant

54
00:03:51,831 --> 00:03:53,816
it with extreme consideration.

55
00:03:54,267 --> 00:03:59,017
Save stores the role and returns to the list, with a confirmation message.

56
00:03:59,475 --> 00:04:02,146
Open Proofreader again to check the result.

57
00:04:02,146 --> 00:04:05,962
Hovering the Effective box of View all content shows the reason:

58
00:04:05,962 --> 00:04:08,525
it is implied by Edit content for others.

59
00:04:12,732 --> 00:04:14,905
Roles are given to users.

60
00:04:14,905 --> 00:04:19,882
Under Access Control, Users, Add User opens the Create User page.

61
00:04:20,337 --> 00:04:23,063
Enter a user name and an email address.

62
00:04:23,063 --> 00:04:28,877
Generate password fills in the password and its confirmation, so nobody has to invent one.

63
00:04:29,333 --> 00:04:32,051
The Roles field lists the roles you can give.

64
00:04:32,051 --> 00:04:36,528
Anonymous and Authenticated are not offered, because they apply automatically.

65
00:04:36,528 --> 00:04:38,073
Let's tick Proofreader.

66
00:04:38,534 --> 00:04:42,850
Save creates the user, and the list shows Proofreader on the user's row.

67
00:04:42,850 --> 00:04:47,554
The same field appears when you edit a user, and a user can have several roles.

68
00:04:51,765 --> 00:04:55,538
Back on the Roles page, let's remove a role we no longer need.

69
00:04:55,538 --> 00:04:59,755
Guest Blogger has a Delete button, and a dialog asks for confirmation.

70
00:05:00,212 --> 00:05:04,188
Choosing Ok deletes the role and shows a confirmation message.

71
00:05:04,188 --> 00:05:06,352
Users who had the role lose it.

72
00:05:10,552 --> 00:05:11,467
To sum up:

73
00:05:11,467 --> 00:05:14,957
permissions belong to roles, and roles belong to users.

74
00:05:14,957 --> 00:05:20,563
Allow grants a permission explicitly, Effective shows the full result, and Security Critical

75
00:05:20,563 --> 00:05:23,252
marks the permissions to grant with care.

76
00:05:25,252 --> 00:05:28,543
Roles and permissions decide who can do what on your site.

77
00:05:28,543 --> 00:05:32,760
A separate video covers permissions for each content type, and for the owner

78
00:05:32,760 --> 00:05:33,995
of a content item.

79
00:05:33,995 --> 00:05:35,332
Thanks for watching.

